hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"166","Al-Hasan bin Muhammad narrated to us, Affan bin Muslim narrated to us, and Saeed bin Mansour narrated to us, they said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Yusuf bin Mahak, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, lagged behind us on a journey we were on, and we found ourselves exhausted. The prayer is the afternoon prayer. While we were performing ablution, he made us wipe our feet. Then he called out in his loudest voice two or three times: “Woe to the heels of the Fire.” This is the wording of the hadith of Affan bin Muslim"
